1
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:29,897
Every time the rain no longer falls, and I
see the sky, I think the rain is falling.

2
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:35,020
Back to when I was a
child, who could only cry,

3
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:37,560
blindly chasing after him.

4
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:45,400
I fell far behind my only thought,
one day I will be stronger.

5
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:50,600
Brideary and gratitude
fading with the wind.

6
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:55,337
Am I stronger now than I was
before, or as weak as back then?

7
00:00:55,420 --> 00:01:01,157
I don't know for sure, but until
I do, my voyage will not end.

8
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:06,340
No matter what's next, I'm
walking straight ahead!

9
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:12,577
So let's go, there's nothing
that can stop us now!

10
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:17,560
Though time's all on our side,
we'll never let it pull us down.

11
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:22,557
And we may fall, but we'll
always keep on standing.

12
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:28,737
There's no way anything will take
what I hold dear away from me!

13
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:33,657
The voices inside me push
me to keep surviving.

14
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:39,257
I'll go on, I'll get through,
no matter what I gotta do!

15
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:43,177
The fiercest of all can pour upon me.

16
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:48,760
I don't care why in the
world would I turn back!

17
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:54,277
So let's go.

18
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:57,897
There's nothing that can stop us now!

19
00:01:57,980 --> 00:02:02,837
Though time's not on our side,
We'll never let it pull us down.

20
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:04,897
And we may fall.

21
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,837
But we'll always keep on standing.

22
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:14,077
There's no way anything will take
What I hold dear away from me?

23
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:17,620
I know the future's there for us to see.

24
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:29,000
I think my poor heart is
about to go kabalooey!

25
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:30,417
Can't you slow us down somehow?

26
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:31,797
There's gotta be something!

27
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:34,468
What good old wax works
in a time like this?

28
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:38,741
Why are Luffy and the
others falling from the sky?

29
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:40,160
Good question.

30
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:44,071
To figure out what happened,
we'll have to go back in time.

31
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:02,937
The waves stopped moving.

32
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:04,917
How in the world did that happen?

33
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,857
That is messed up.

34
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:09,897
I mean, at least we're not dead.

35
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:11,317
But what are we supposed to do?

36
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,877
Take an ice pick to this thing.

37
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,817
I think I know who.

38
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:16,180
You did this as well.

39
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,820
Just take a look below.

40
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:23,140
The answer's clear enough.

41
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:26,040
It's the old man.

42
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:28,653
The battle's already started without us.

43
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:30,280
It's just as I thought.

44
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:33,033
I got an idea that'll get us down there.

45
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:35,497
We got less than three hours to work with,

46
00:03:35,580 --> 00:03:38,877
so this is our best chance to
save Ace from getting executed.

47
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:40,080
Uh-huh, go on.

48
00:03:40,580 --> 00:03:41,780
Are you mad?

49
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:46,277
You want to slide all the way down
this frozen wave back into the sea?

50
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,190
That's it.

51
00:03:47,273 --> 00:03:50,897
But first, we gotta wiggle the ship
free so we can actually start sliding.

52
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:53,137
Need I remind you, this is a battleship.

53
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:54,777
It's not going to wiggle easily.

54
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:56,566
Did you hear that, you idiot?

55
00:03:56,820 --> 00:04:00,580
If we work together, I know we can do it.

56
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:03,777
When you put it that way,
it sounds pretty cool.

57
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:04,690
Oh, right.

58
00:04:04,773 --> 00:04:06,517
If Captain Buggy, the
next king of the pirates,

59
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:08,457
thinks we can do it,
then anything's possible.

60
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:10,697
His fighting spirit is rubbing off on us!

61
00:04:10,780 --> 00:04:13,020
Buggy's the best captain ever! Yeah!

62
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:18,221
Attention all ships and soldiers.

63
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:20,720
A new target is T-O-T-T-Z.

64
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:24,277
Commence change in formation and
make the shift to Operation 3.

65
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:26,557
Sounds like the Navy is
busy giving out orders.

66
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:29,260
Advance all preparations now. Daddy?

67
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:30,957
What do you think that means?

68
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:31,870
Dunno.

69
00:04:31,953 --> 00:04:33,757
Maybe some sort of secret
code they're using.

70
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:35,217
Once all soldiers are in place,

71
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:38,457
we will move the schedule forward
and execute Ace immediately.

72
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:39,920
That is all, Colby. No!

73
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:45,500
Luffy, no. Let's move!

74
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:47,407
There's no time for arguing.

75
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:49,364
We can't bum around any longer.

76
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:53,033
Everyone, follow Strawboy's
lead and help move this ship.

77
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:56,740
Let's go!

78
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,040
Wait a minute.

79
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:06,970
No!

80
00:05:07,053 --> 00:05:08,180
Let's go on fly!

81
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:16,540
And that is how Luffy and the others
ended up falling from the sky.

82
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:51,040
Did that really happen?

83
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:54,319
A navy ship fell out of the
sky like it was nothing!

84
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:56,800
Water! It's water!

85
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:58,433
I thought we were dead!

86
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:02,197
I figured we'd all be goners once
the ship crashed into the ice.

87
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:04,480
Hey, why isn't it frozen here?

88
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:05,970
Gradrolls!

89
00:06:06,053 --> 00:06:07,180
Start climbing! Ha!

90
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:11,968
This ain't got nothing on the water
torture we went through and impelled down!

91
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:23,760
What use are Devil Fruit
powers if you can't even swim?

92
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:00,720
Oh, my God.

93
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:07,870
LUMBAYS!

94
00:07:07,953 --> 00:07:08,783
I'M HERE!

95
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:14,470
LUMBAY!

96
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:20,720
Finally found you!

97
00:07:22,260 --> 00:07:23,090
Hey!

98
00:07:23,173 --> 00:07:24,569
Is that who I think it is?

99
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:25,860
It's Crocodile!

100
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:27,897
And he's not the only one either!

101
00:07:27,980 --> 00:07:29,857
Just take a look at that line up!

102
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:31,740
A who's who on both sides!

103
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:33,700
All the big names are here!

104
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:36,800
The world can't handle this madness!

105
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:40,680
Hey Ace, sit tight, okay?

106
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:43,540
Cause we're gonna get you out of here!

107
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:46,640
Hey Garth!

108
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:50,260
Your family's messing
things up again! Fluffy, no!

109
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:53,360
Look, Straw Hat's got some company!

110
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:54,780
It's Jinbei!

111
00:07:55,020 --> 00:07:57,217
And the Revolutionary Army's at Bonkong!

112
00:07:57,300 --> 00:08:00,241
There's a ton of infamous
pirates behind them too!

113
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:03,520
They must have all escaped
from Impel Down somehow!

114
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:06,832
Straw Hat's causing trouble again, is he?

115
00:08:07,060 --> 00:08:08,300
I'm not surprised.

116
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:11,520
Is that Straw Hat?

117
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,400
What is Straw Hat Luffy doing here, too?

118
00:08:14,900 --> 00:08:17,537
Looks like he forgot to bring
his crew along with him.

119
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:20,720
Luffy, I'm so relieved
to see that you're alive.

120
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:23,980
I can't believe it, Helmepo! What is it?

121
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:25,786
Not another surprise, I hope.

122
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:28,580
Straw Hat! That's crazy!

123
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,957
That means he must have
escaped from Impel Down!

124
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,617
How much tougher can this guy get?

125
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:35,660
Now those are some big
fish we're staring at.

126
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:39,700
Well, fancy seeing him.

127
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:41,900
That boy sure gets around, huh?

128
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:45,677
Guess that's the famous kid brother
Ace was always telling us about.

129
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:48,400
A former and active warlord hand in hand!

130
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:50,520
And look!

131
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:54,017
We even have the famous rookie
Straw Hat in attendance!

132
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:55,160
This is too good!

133
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:56,538
Smoker, look there!

134
00:08:56,660 --> 00:08:57,490
Quickly!

135
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:58,680
Eat this!

136
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:08,220
Straw Hat Luthien Crocodile what are
those two doing together so it is him

137
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:11,697
The grandson of our very own Marine Hero

138
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:15,220
Guard and the son of
the Revolutionary Dragon

139
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:21,100
I'll make that boy regret the
day he decided to become a pirate

140
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:30,520
Of all things, you have the goal to
allow yourself a Straw Hat, Luffy.

141
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:34,157
After all we've done for you,
you're a payage like this!

142
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,070
That's right!

143
00:09:35,153 --> 00:09:37,489
I choose to resign from
the seven warlords!

144
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:41,940
Rather peculiar, all these
groups uniting against us.

145
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:45,827
I highly doubt everyone here has
a common goal in this battle.

146
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:49,138
They're all too different
for that to make any sense.

147
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:04,040
Where'd Crocoboy go?

148
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:08,172
I guess the sucker chickened
out and left us high and dry.

149
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:09,780
Wait, there he is!

150
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:15,813
Damn it, you're supposed to wait for me!

151
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:18,340
It's Crocodile!

152
00:10:18,460 --> 00:10:19,657
He's going straight for Whitebeard!

153
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:23,520
Long time no see, old man.

154
00:10:23,900 --> 00:10:25,760
You never learn.

155
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:55,440
straw that knows too well what my strengths
and weaknesses are once you touch water

156
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,995
Then you can't turn into sand anymore.

157
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:06,100
You know, there's only
one reason I'm here.

158
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:09,577
If you want to save your brother
so bad, stay out of my way.

159
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:12,307
I'm killing Whitebeard
and you can't stop me.

160
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:13,897
So that old guy is Whitebeard.

161
00:11:13,980 --> 00:11:14,810
I thought so.

162
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:16,392
Just stay away from him.

163
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:19,617
He's Ace's friend, so I'm not
going to let him get hurt.

164
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:21,257
Well, would you look at that?

165
00:11:21,340 --> 00:11:22,634
It runs in the family.

166
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:26,200
Don't let him get close to Pops!

167
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:44,642
When you came back from
East Blue missing an arm,

168
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:46,977
you better believe the rumors were flying.

169
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:49,020
I was pretty curious myself.

170
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:54,520
Now I can ask you face to face, what
enemy did you give that left arm to?

171
00:11:58,100 --> 00:12:02,220
Don't worry, I gave it to a kid.

172
00:12:02,780 --> 00:12:05,820
Hey Squirt, that straw
hat that you're wearing,

173
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:10,220
it looks exactly like the one
red-haired Shanks used to have on him.

174
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:13,217
Hold on, how do you and
Shanks know each other?

175
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:16,065
You're right, it was his
hat, he left it to me.

176
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:20,600
Can you believe it pops look
this dork is my kid brother

177
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:28,260
You came here to rescue your
big brother, that's right.

178
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:32,008
Do you have the slightest idea
who our forces are up against?

179
00:12:36,980 --> 00:12:40,480
A squirt like you is gonna
get slaughtered real easy.

180
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:45,000
Shut up, you don't know
you don't even know me?

181
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:48,420
I know what you're up to.

182
00:12:48,820 --> 00:12:51,000
Yeah, you want to be the king, huh?

183
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:55,080
First, you've got to go
through me. Got it! Got it!

184
00:12:55,220 --> 00:12:56,080
Got it!

185
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:58,000
Got it! Got it!

186
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:22,640
What a cheeky little punk.

187
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:27,937
Don't come crying to me for help if
you get a few boo-boos, spoiled brat.

188
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:28,850
Yeah, right.

189
00:13:28,933 --> 00:13:30,271
I'm not all old like you.

190
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:35,135
I'm going to be the one to rescue Ace.

191
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:37,560
He's competing. With what?

192
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:39,320
We're done for.

193
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:48,520
How cute.

194
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:51,645
I would assume this is
all punishable by death.

195
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:52,840
Right, Sengoku?

196
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:55,850
Definitely.

197
00:13:55,933 --> 00:13:59,077
They're throwing out the schedule
for an immediate execution.

198
00:13:59,160 --> 00:14:01,577
Are you positive that's
what you heard them say?

199
00:14:01,660 --> 00:14:04,657
Yeah, they said they got to get all
set for something first, though.

200
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:07,677
But I don't know what for,
because they were using codes.

201
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:12,340
I think you want to rescue Ace as bad
as me, and that's why I'm telling you.

202
00:14:12,980 --> 00:14:14,400
Well, all right.

203
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:16,877
I suppose it's lucky I ran into you then.

204
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:20,060
Thanks, kiddo. Sure thing. No big deal.

205
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:22,957
Now he's talking like they're equals!

206
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:25,158
That boy has got some serious balls!

207
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:27,110
Right!

208
00:14:27,193 --> 00:14:28,023
Hang on, Ace!

209
00:14:28,106 --> 00:14:28,936
I'm on my way!

210
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:33,020
And there he goes.

211
00:14:41,780 --> 00:14:43,740
Get out of my way.

212
00:14:44,620 --> 00:14:46,597
Well, he's Ace's brother, all right!

213
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:49,077
Third division, let's get moving.

214
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:51,984
Keep up with the boy and
try to follow his lead.

215
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,380
Let's lend our support. What?

216
00:14:58,220 --> 00:14:59,200
Come on!

217
00:15:02,460 --> 00:15:03,420
14th Division!

218
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:05,020
Let's clear a path!

219
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:07,266
We're right behind you, boss!

220
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:11,750
Luffy.

221
00:15:12,460 --> 00:15:15,117
One rookie daredevil
suddenly takes the lead

222
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:17,537
and they're acting like a whole new army.

223
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:18,796
Not that it matters.

224
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:20,351
Our strategy is airtight.

225
00:15:21,800 --> 00:15:22,630
Don't hesitate!

226
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:23,960
Follow my orders!

227
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:27,240
So typical of Sengoku,

228
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:29,917
he probably doesn't
think the execution of a

229
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,497
mere pirate deserves the
formality of a schedule.

230
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:35,992
The big question is what they're
getting set up for first?

231
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:39,760
Hey Pops,

232
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:41,077
just in case you haven't heard,

233
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:43,717
word on the street is they're
expediting Ace's execution!

234
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:45,540
Straw Hat told me.

235
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:50,417
Something in my gut tells me Sengoku
wanted us to get that leaked info.

236
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:52,920
He wants us to advance. Huh?

237
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:57,032
That old bastard's too clever
to let his strategy get out.

238
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,940
Not that easily, at least.

239
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:01,081
He's many things, but not a fool.

240
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:03,100
Everybody climb!

241
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:08,700
A lightspeed kick?

242
00:16:11,520 --> 00:16:13,814
Did you think I was gonna let you pass?

243
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:17,860
You fellas are awfully confident
for a bunch of nobodies. Damn!

244
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:19,520
It's Admiral Kizaru!

245
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,430
Huh?

246
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:24,400
Hey, you're that jerk from Saboori!

247
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:28,542
And you're the boy the Celestial
Dragons asked me to take care of.

248
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:32,460
Nice to get a second chance.

249
00:16:34,580 --> 00:16:35,410
Crap!

250
00:16:35,493 --> 00:16:37,160
Straw Hat's out of his boy!

251
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:39,600
Death win!

252
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:50,880
Ah, please!

253
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,880
I want to go home! What?

254
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:54,820
Whoa, Captain Buggy!

255
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:57,391
Wow, I knew you were gutted, but hot damn!

256
00:16:58,340 --> 00:17:00,740
You mean you want to kill Kizaru, right?

257
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:02,260
